					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/owarinozeref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6976987); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6976987&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606489185" alt="OwariNoZeref" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6976987)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/owarinozeref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6976987); return false;" >OwariNoZeref</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606359448 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 02:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828238">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An anomalous snow globe that contains a fully functional society of individuals who have been transported into it. The victims of the globe are almost instantaneously erased from all historical records and human memory.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In December, 2019, a low level foundation member purchased a snow globe from a Christmas shop to gift his significant other. It caught his eye because of the realistic landscape of the snow globe, but when the gift was opened a half a month later, there were certain features that had appeared on the landscape that the foundation member were not there when he purchased the globe, such as a crop field and a few crude houses. The foundation personnel brought the globe to the foundation and has since been on 24-hour observation by a camera which has documented the progress of the internal civilization.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>While on a routine sweep of the Alaskan Bush, a foundation team reported the immediate disappearance of a team member, as if he had been swallowed up by the air in front of him. As foundation command began to question the team on the specifics of the disappearance immediately following the incident, they could no longer recall the existence of the team member at all, and foundation records of the team suggested likewise. The identification of a disappearance was nonetheless recorded. The anomalous properties of the snow globe were only discovered when the camera observing the snow globe recorded a flare gun fire from within the forest of the globe approximately 3 minutes after the disappearance of the team member. Currently no attempts have been made from the inhabitants of the interior to communicate with the foundation, and it is unknown whether the victims are aware of their situation. When foundation personnel revisited the site of the disappearance, nothing occurred, and the source of victimization remains unknown.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> While the idea of a miniature self-contained civilization isn’t completely unique, the events that resulted in the discovery of the anomaly is testament to the aptitude of the foundation. Someone had to be curious enough, or the foundation is thorough enough, that the cross reference between the report of the disappearance and the observation of the flare within the globe was able to occur. Regardless, it was a fun and engaging idea to develop.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I’m open to ideas on making the civilization itself more engaging, but I think the disconnect between the inhabitants of the globe and the foundation is interesting on its own. I’m also considering including a label that says SCP Foundation, which would allude that the globe might be a failed experiment and/or one from another reality.</p>
</div>
</div>
