				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606489185" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;" >Grigori Karpin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606454636 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Nov 2020 05:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829144">
									

<p>This:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The victims of the globe are almost instantaneously erased from all historical records and human memory.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is inconsistent with this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a foundation team reported the immediate disappearance of a team member, as if he had been swallowed up by the air in front of him. As foundation command began to question the team on the specifics of the disappearance immediately following the incident, they could not recall the existence of the team member at all, and foundation records of the team suggested likewise. The identification of a disappearance was nonetheless recorded.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>if the victim instantaneously disappears from human memory and records, then the agent wouldn’t have noticed. Depending on how strong the editing is, maybe even if there was footage of the victim’s disappearance, that too would be erased. You see what I mean?</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Someone had to be curious enough, or the foundation is thorough enough, that the cross reference between the report of the disappearance and the observation of the flare within the globe was able to occur.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>as noted above, there wouldn’t necessarily be a way to tell this from footage&#8230; you have to discern the strength of the reality warping this item would create.</em></p>
<ul>
<li>there’s not much in the way of a narrative here. This is “strange thing’s details” and “vaguely how it is discovered”</li>
</ul>
<p>What will the overall arc of the narrative be? Novelty of the anomaly is not enough to engage usually because it’s hard to really make a novel anomaly. Instead the focus should be on how you’ll craft your story.</p>
<p>So what’s the article about, besides the discovery? If it’s solely about the anomalous nature of the item, that isn’t a narrative, that’s an entry in a D&amp;D rule book. Why do you find this interesting? What will engage the reader in your story?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
							</div>

								
